<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- THE STORE CHANNEL — Google Play (and any other store we later submit
         to). ST-1, 2026-08-19.

         🔴 THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF PERMISSIONS, AND THE EMPTINESS IS
         THE FEATURE. `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` lives in the direct flavour
         only, so a store artifact cannot declare it — not because someone
         remembered to strip it, but because it was never merged in. Play's
         Device and Network Abuse policy forbids a store-delivered app from
         downloading and installing an APK to update itself, and a restricted
         permission in the manifest is reviewed whether or not any code uses it.

         ⚠️ DO NOT "TIDY THIS FILE AWAY". An empty flavour manifest looks like
         dead weight and is not: deleting it removes the place where the next
         person reads why the two channels differ. If a store-only permission
         is ever needed, it goes here — and its absence from the direct flavour
         then needs the same kind of paragraph.

         The runtime half of the same rule is lib/src/update/install_source.dart
         (gate ②): even in a mis-built artifact, an app that Play installed
         refuses to install an update itself. Two independent mechanisms,
         because the build one is ours to get wrong and the runtime one is
         mechanical. -->
</manifest>
